From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jose Martins <josemartins90@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 22:13:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/13] drivers: imsic: add S-mode support gated on
 CONFIG_RISCV_S_MODE
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The IMSIC driver was M-mode only. Add S-mode support suitable for guests
running under a hypervisor (e.g. Bao) that configure Zephyr with
CONFIG_RISCV_S_MODE.

Per AIA spec §3.7, the indirect interrupt-file register map (eidelivery,
eithreshold, eip*, eie*) is identical at all privilege levels. Only the
selector/access CSRs and the *topei claim CSR differ:
  - M-level: miselect/mireg, mtopei (0x35C)
  - S-level: siselect/sireg, stopei (0x15C)

Changes:

icsr.h: Add sicsr_read/write/set/clear/read_set/read_clear helpers
  gated on CONFIG_RISCV_ISA_EXT_SMCSRIND && CONFIG_RISCV_S_MODE.
  The Sscsrind extension is not yet modelled in Zephyr's Kconfig, so
  reuse the Smcsrind guard (same hardware base, different privilege).

irq.h: Add RISCV_IRQ_SEXT = 9 (supervisor external interrupt cause).

riscv_imsic.h: Add CSR_STOPEI (0x15C), CSR_STOPI (0xDB0), and
  TOPEI_EIID_SHIFT/MASK for the *topei field format (AIA §3.9, EIID
  in bits [26:16]).  Also fix riscv_imsic_claim: the previous code
  masked topei without first shifting right 16, returning a garbage
  value that mixes priority bits into the interrupt identity.

intc_riscv_imsic.c: Introduce xcsr_*/CSR_XTOPEI/RISCV_IRQ_XEXT macros
  that resolve to the appropriate privilege-level accessors at compile
  time. All driver logic (init, enable, disable, claim, secondary CPU
  init) now uses these abstractions unchanged for both M and S mode.

Signed-off-by: Jose Martins <josemartins90@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 6eae776afc50f4ad3fcebe84ace9132d38fbde49)
---
